# Data integration rules

These rules apply to import pipeline, Gmail sync, search, and all cron/background work.

## Gmail sync

Full spec: `docs/specs/gmail-sync.md`

- Ecosystem owns Gmail sync. Not shared with Pathway PM (ADR 0007).
- Sync code lives in `src/lib/integrations/gmail/`.
- Cron endpoint: `src/app/api/cron/gmail-sync/route.ts`. Verify `CRON_SECRET` header before processing.
- Use `createAdminClient()` (service role) for sync writes. Set `org_id` explicitly on every insert.
- Label filter: read from `GMAIL_SYNC_LABELS` env var. Never hard-code label names.
- Upsert on `(org_id, gmail_thread_id)` and `(org_id, gmail_message_id)`. Never insert duplicates.
- On participant match: generate activity + append relationship_source. Skip if `source_ref` already exists.
- On no match: create `email_participant_reviews` row with `status=pending`. Never auto-create a profile from email ingestion.
- Backfill runs once on account connect (12 months). Incremental sync daily from `sync_cursor`.

## Import pipeline

Full spec: `docs/specs/import-pipeline.md`

- Pipeline stages: Upload → Parse → Preview → Map → Dedup → Review → Commit → Audit.
- Staged rows in `import_rows` table. Never stage in jsonb metadata for row-level dedup.
- Dedup tier 1: email exact match → `matched_email` → update existing profile (fill empty fields only, never overwrite).
- Dedup tier 2: `lower(full_name) + lower(organisation_name)` → `soft_match` → admin review required.
- Dedup tier 3: no match → `new` → create profile.
- Never auto-merge on name alone (ADR 0004).
- Commit is atomic (database transaction). If any step fails, roll back the transaction.
- Retain `import_rows` after commit for audit trail. Do not delete staging rows.
- File limits: 10 MB, 5,000 rows. Enforce at upload.

## Search

Full spec: `docs/specs/search.md`

- Phase 1: Postgres FTS only. No external search service, no pgvector until Phase 2.
- Each indexed table has a generated `fts tsvector` column and a GIN index.
- Cross-entity search: parallel queries per entity type, merged in `src/lib/computed/search.ts`.
- Body search (`email_messages.fts`) is a separate query path. Never include in the general search view.
- Use `plainto_tsquery` (AND semantics) for user input. Use `ts_rank_cd` for ranking.
- Empty query → return nothing. Never return all rows on an empty search.

## Layer 2 computed values

- Orbit ring, relationship strength, last_interaction, connect suggestions: implement as SQL views in `supabase/migrations/` or query-time functions in `src/lib/computed/`.
- Never store a computed value in a user-editable column. If a formula changes, update the view — no migration required.
- Source columns (`source`, `source_ref`) must be present on every ingested record. Do not omit.

## Cron discipline

- All cron endpoints: verify `CRON_SECRET`. Return 401 if missing or wrong.
- Use `createAdminClient()` only in `api/cron/` and `lib/integrations/`. Never import it from UI code.
- Log each run: account/job processed, rows affected, errors.
- Idempotent by design. Cron failure and retry must not produce duplicate data.
